== 1.7 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Accounting is best defined as the process of],
  [auditing the books of a company],
  [identifying, recording, summarising and communicating financial information],
  [recording cash receipts only],
  [preparing a trial balance]
)

#mcq(2, [Bookkeeping differs from accounting because bookkeeping],
  [includes interpretation of accounts],
  [stops at recording and classifying],
  [is done only by auditors],
  [is illegal for small firms]
)

#mcq(3, [Which is NOT a user of accounting information?],
  [an employee's union],
  [a competitor's customer],
  [the tax authority],
  [a bank considering a loan]
)

#mcq(4, [The business entity concept requires that],
  [the owner's private affairs be kept out of the books],
  [profit be recognised when cash is received],
  [the business continue forever],
  [assets be valued at market price]
)

#mcq(5, [Valuing assets on the assumption that the firm will continue in business is the],
  [materiality concept],
  [going concern concept],
  [realisation concept],
  [prudence concept]
)

#mcq(6, [Recording an expense in the period it relates to, not when it is paid, is the],
  [accruals concept],
  [cash basis],
  [entity concept],
  [consistency concept]
)

#mcq(7, [Using the same depreciation method every year applies the],
  [money measurement concept],
  [realisation concept],
  [prudence concept],
  [consistency concept]
)

#mcq(8, [Providing for doubtful debts is an application of],
  [prudence],
  [consistency],
  [materiality],
  [realisation]
)

#mcq(9, [Revenue is recognised when the sale is made and the goods pass, under the],
  [going concern concept],
  [accruals concept],
  [entity concept],
  [realisation concept]
)

#mcq(10, [Treating a ₦2,000 stapler as an expense rather than a fixed asset applies],
  [materiality],
  [objectivity],
  [prudence],
  [consistency]
)

#mcq(11, [A skilled workforce is not shown as an asset because of the],
  [money measurement concept],
  [accruals concept],
  [consistency concept],
  [realisation concept]
)

#mcq(12, [Recording assets at what they cost rather than at market value applies],
  [prudence],
  [historical cost],
  [materiality],
  [realisation]
)

#mcq(13, [Every entry must rest on evidence an independent person can check. This is],
  [consistency],
  [materiality],
  [objectivity],
  [going concern]
)

#mcq(14, [Financial accounting is prepared mainly for],
  [the costing department],
  [users outside the firm],
  [managers inside the firm],
  [the factory supervisor]
)

#mcq(15, [Management accounting is distinguished by its],
  [compliance with the Companies Act],
  [annual reporting cycle],
  [publication in the annual report],
  [focus on the future and internal decisions]
)

#mcq(16, [Cost accounting is chiefly concerned with],
  [the audit of the cash book],
  [the valuation of shares],
  [the cost of a product, job or process],
  [the tax liability of a company]
)

#mcq(17, [An audit report expresses an opinion on whether the accounts],
  [show a profit],
  [have been filed on time],
  [give a true and fair view],
  [are free of fraud]
)

#mcq(18, [The body that sets financial reporting standards in Nigeria is the],
  [FRCN],
  [NDIC],
  [CAC],
  [CBN]
)

#mcq(19, [The professional body of accountants in Nigeria is the],
  [ICAN],
  [MAN],
  [NBA],
  [NSE]
)

#mcq(20, [Money taken from the business by its owner for private use is],
  [a liability],
  [drawings],
  [an expense],
  [a loan to the owner]
)

#mcq(21, [Capital introduced by the owner],
  [is recorded as income],
  [reduces liabilities],
  [increases capital and increases assets],
  [increases profit]
)

#mcq(22, [Accounting information that makes a difference to a decision is],
  [relevant],
  [material],
  [comparable],
  [reliable]
)

#mcq(23, [The quality that allows one firm's accounts to be set beside another's is],
  [materiality],
  [relevance],
  [comparability],
  [prudence]
)

#mcq(24, [Information free from bias and material error is],
  [relevant],
  [concise],
  [reliable],
  [timely]
)

#mcq(25, [A provision for doubtful debts is justified by],
  [entity],
  [going concern],
  [realisation],
  [prudence]
)

#mcq(26, [Depreciating a machine over its useful life applies the],
  [realisation concept],
  [entity concept],
  [money measurement concept],
  [accruals concept]
)

#mcq(27, [A firm that changes its stock valuation method whenever profit falls is violating],
  [prudence],
  [realisation],
  [materiality],
  [consistency]
)

#mcq(28, [The periodicity concept assumes that],
  [the business will continue],
  [prices are stable],
  [accounts can be prepared for artificial periods],
  [all income is cash]
)

#mcq(29, [The dual aspect concept is the basis of],
  [double entry],
  [the trial balance only],
  [the cash book only],
  [the audit]
)

#mcq(30, [The statement that shows the financial position at a date is the],
  [profit and loss account],
  [cash flow forecast],
  [trading account],
  [balance sheet]
)

#mcq(31, [The statement that shows performance over a period is the],
  [statement of affairs],
  [trial balance],
  [balance sheet],
  [profit and loss account]
)

#mcq(32, [Owner's equity is equal to],
  [current assets minus stock],
  [assets minus liabilities],
  [liabilities minus assets],
  [assets plus liabilities]
)

#mcq(33, [Which user is internal?],
  [a bank],
  [the tax office],
  [a supplier],
  [the production manager]
)

#mcq(34, [Which user is most interested in the firm's ability to repay a loan?],
  [a lender],
  [the public],
  [a customer],
  [an employee]
)

#mcq(35, [The main purpose of accounting information is to],
  [reduce tax],
  [increase sales],
  [support economic decisions],
  [satisfy the law]
)

#mcq(36, [Which pair is correctly matched?],
  [going concern: assets at break-up value],
  [realisation: provision for doubtful debts],
  [materiality: small items expensed],
  [prudence: recognise revenue when goods are delivered]
)

#mcq(37, [A business pays the owner's house rent from its bank account. The correct treatment is],
  [drawings],
  [rent expense],
  [a liability],
  [a loan to the owner]
)

#mcq(38, [Accounting is called the language of business because it],
  [replaces the law],
  [is spoken in meetings],
  [communicates financial information to users],
  [uses English]
)

#mcq(39, [Which is a limitation of historical cost accounting?],
  [it ignores changes in the value of money],
  [it is objective],
  [it relies on documents],
  [it is verifiable]
)

#mcq(40, [Which concept explains why the owner's private house is not shown in the business balance sheet?],
  [materiality],
  [going concern],
  [realisation],
  [business entity]
)

